Shows the shipping-methods loader only when the debounced rates estimation actually starts
and shortens the debounce (MGS-5715).

Root cause 1: bindHandler() turns on shippingService.isLoading() synchronously on every
value change of an observed address field, but the actual validation and the
estimate-shipping-methods request are deferred by validateDelay. Users see a loader for the
whole debounce period after each keystroke before any request is sent.
Fix: isLoading(true) is moved into the delayed callback, right before validateFields(),
so the loader appears together with the request. validateFields() and the rate processors
still turn it off on their own.

Root cause 2: validateDelay of 2000 ms adds up to two seconds of idle wait after the last
keystroke before rates are requested.
Fix: validateDelay lowered to 600 ms, enough to absorb typing pauses while keeping the
rates refresh close to one second after the user stops typing.

